# Code Organization Guidelines

## Directory Structure
- `src/lib/`: Core utilities and configuration
  - [src/lib/config.ts](mdc:src/lib/config.ts): Central configuration management
- `src/integrations/`: External service integrations
  - `src/integrations/supabase/`: Supabase-specific code
- `src/contexts/`: React context providers
- `src/services/`: Business logic and data access
- `src/components/`: React components

## Configuration Management
- Environment variables are managed through [src/lib/config.ts](mdc:src/lib/config.ts)
- Use the `getEnv()` helper for accessing environment variables
- Configuration is organized by feature (payment, Supabase, etc.)

## Integration Patterns
- Keep external service integrations isolated in `src/integrations/`
- Use typed clients and interfaces
- Handle errors consistently
- Implement proper error boundaries

## Best Practices
- Follow DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principles
- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Keep components focused and single-responsibility
- Implement proper error handling and logging
- Use environment-specific configuration

